load_inline: name includes version; set build directory default (~/.cache/torch_extensions) on box. Compile once at import; eval imports module fresh each run (tempfile import), but extension cache persists across runs → rebuild only when source changes. Since final verification runs in a separate environment (fresh box from task image!), the extension will compile during import there... The final verifier runs evaluate.py → load_custom_model_with_tempfile → exec_module → triggers load_inline compile (1-2 min?) on their box. That's probably acceptable (correctness first, compile happens before timing). But risk: if their box lacks nvcc? The task image includes nvcc presumably (same image). OK.

