CUDA path is likely faster than triton for this. But triton is safer for final env (no nvcc dependency). The image has nvcc (it's the same image). I'll go CUDA primary; could add triton fallback... keep it simple but robust: try CUDA load_inline; if it fails at import, fall back to a triton or pure-torch implementation. Actually a fallback adds code complexity; but insurance for correctness > speed (score 0 if incorrect/compile fail). Let me add try/except around load_inline, with fallback to torch native layer_norm (F.layer_norm) — never incorrect.

